  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Joju M.L vs State Of Kerala on 23 September, 2024 Author: Dinesh Kumar Singh Bench: Dinesh Kumar Singh Wp(C) No. 27959 Of 2023 1 2024:Ker:70645 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice Dinesh Kumar Singh Monday, The 23Rd Day Of September 2024 / 1St Aswina, 1946 Wp(C) No. 27959 Of 2023 Petitioners: 1 Joju M.L., Aged 47 Years S/O C.D Lona, Masliyakkel Chettakkada House, Vellikulam Road, North Chalakudy, Thrissur, Pin - 680307 2 Merchant'S Association, Chalakkudy, Thrissur District, Represented By Its President, Mr. Joy Moothedan, Pin - 680307 3 Mr. Raison Alukka, General Secretary, Merchant'S Association, Chalakkudy,Thrissur District, Pin - 680307 By Adv Asha Babu Respondents: 1 State Of Kerala, Represented By Its Secretary To The Government Local Self Government Department, Secretariat, Thiruvananthapuram, Pin - 695001 2 Chalakudy Municipality, Represented By Its Secretary, Municipal Office, Chalakudy P.O, Thrissur District, Pin - 680307 Joju M.L vs State Of Kerala on 23 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/76234215/ 1 3 Secretary, Chalakudy Municipality, Municipal Office, Chalakudy P.O, Thrissur District, Pin - 680307 4 Food Safety Officer, Food Safety Department, Chalakudy Circle, Thrissur District, Pin - 680307 5 Majeed B.A., Wp(C) No. 27959 Of 2023 2 2024:Ker:70645 Bunglowparambil House, Vettukadavu, Chalakkudy P.O., Thrissur District, Pin - 680307 By Advs. Shri.Sheejo Chacko, Sc, Chalakudy Municipality Lindons C.Davis E.U.Dhanya V.C.Valsan N.S.Shamila Chinju P. Joyies THIS WRIT PETITION (CIVIL) HAVING COME UP FOR ADMISSION ON 23.09.2024, THE COURT ON THE SAME DAY DELIVERED THE FOLLOWING: WP(C) NO. 27959 OF 2023 3 2024:KER:70645 JUDGMENT Dated this the 23rd day of September, 2024",
    "facts": "The 1 st petitioner is occupying in Building No.FS28 as per valid license in ward No.XIX of the Chalakudy market complex on the basis of an agreement executed with the 2 nd respondent Municipality. 2. The allegation in the writ petition is that the 5 th respondent is carrying on illegal vending of dry fish on a cart in the Chalakudy market and despite the complainnt given to the Municipal authorities, no action has been taken to remove the 5 th respondent from the Chalakudy market inasmuch as the 5th respondent does not have any valid license to vend in the Chalakudy market. The petitioners have approached this Court with the present writ petition seeking a writ of mandamus/direction commanding the Municipal authorities to remove all illegal traders from WP(C) NO. 27959 OF 2023 2024:KER:70645 Chalakudy market premises including the 5 th Joju M.L vs State Of Kerala on 23 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/76234215/ 2 respondent. 3.",
    "arguments": "However, the Municipality has not taken WP(C) NO. 27959 OF 2023 2024:KER:70645 any steps to identify the vending zone for the street vendors like the 5th respondent, despite more than 9 years have elapsed since the judgment passed by this Court on 23.01.2015. The 5th respondent has also prayed for a direction to the Municipal authorities to take appropriate action to implement plan for street vending as per Section 21 read with first schedule and Promotional measures as per Section 31 of Street Vendors (Protection of Livelihood and Regulation of Street Vending) Act in Chalakudy Municipality."
  },
